       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to **7,650 mg/day**. That is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of 2,550 mg/day. A dose that high risks severe lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **2,550 mg total per day**, divided differently, such as 1,000 mg BID or 500 mg TID.\n- A lower starting dose, such as 500 mg PO BID with meals. Metformin is usually started low and titrated up to limit GI side effects.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and check it with your resident or attending. Once you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
